Subject: [PATCH] fonts: a Windows persona answers the names Windows aliases

Stock Windows Chrome reports Courier, Helvetica, Times, MS Sans Serif, MS
Serif, Franklin Gothic and Arial Narrow as present, measuring as Courier New,
Arial, Times New Roman, Microsoft Sans Serif, Times New Roman, Franklin
Gothic Medium and Arial. A Windows persona hid them all. It now runs the
Windows name mapping on any host, and on Linux also answers Helvetica with
Arial, a name without its weight word with the listed family (Franklin Gothic
Medium), and a width name whose narrow face is not listed with the base family
at normal width. Each name shows exactly when its target is listed, no lookup
returns a host face under the name itself, and src:local() checks names as
listed.

